Z||000000||3fifty||11-26-2001||09:50 PM||||When I bought my 85 2.8 GT Auto it was shifting hard. Then started hanging in 2nd with plenty of fluid. It would go into high<BR>gear every now and then at about 4K. Changed the fluid and filter today. Inside was super clean and no metal on magnet. Is there a vacum or elect item that could affect high gear only, or am I faced with pulling the tranny? <BR>Thanks, 3fifty ||||reg||5
Z||000001||daved||11-26-2001||10:52 PM||||$3.50 LOL<BR>It's most likely your TV cable (page 183 of the Haynes if you have it).  The cable goes from the throttle down to the tranny. It could be just a very simple adjustment, or as in my case the adjuster had broken.  Hope thats it, because it's a real cheap fix.  Otherwise it may mean a new tranny; Good luck||||reg||1
